# EARTHDALE — COMPLETE NPC INTELLIGENCE, SOCIAL SIMULATION & CIVILIZATION PROGRESSION OVERHAUL

## ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior game systems architect, AI simulation engineer, gameplay programmer, and technical designer.

Your task is to evolve the existing **Earthdale** project into a believable, autonomous civilization simulation.

This is an enhancement of an existing game, NOT a request to rebuild the project from scratch.

Preserve existing working mechanics, architecture, assets, and game identity wherever possible. Improve the underlying simulation systems, NPC behavior, world interactions, progression, and multiplayer experience.

The objective is to create a living world where villagers gradually develop intelligence, relationships, knowledge, survival capabilities, culture, and social structures.

## CORE DESIGN PHILOSOPHY

The world must obey consistent rules.

- NPCs must not magically create resources, buildings, knowledge, or population.
- NPCs must have limitations based on their current knowledge, skills, experience, personality, and available resources.
- Relationships must develop through actual interactions and experiences.
- Civilization must progress gradually.
- The environment must physically affect NPC decisions.
- Social behavior must have consequences.
- Every significant event must have a valid simulation cause.
- AI decisions must be explainable and inspectable.
- Every system must be modular, maintainable, and testable.

