# PHASE 11 — MODULAR SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE

Do not implement everything in one enormous NPC controller.

Organize the implementation into independent modules with clear responsibilities.

Suggested logical modules:

| Module | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| NPC Cognition | Decision-making, learning, memory |
| NPC Personality | Individual traits and preferences |
| NPC Needs | Hunger, energy, safety and social needs |
| NPC Memory | Experiences and memory retrieval |
| NPC Social | Relationships and interactions |
| Social Events | Confirmed event generation |
| Resource System | Gathering, depletion and regeneration |
| Inventory | Carrying and storing resources |
| Construction | Building stages and requirements |
| Knowledge System | Learning and skill progression |
| Navigation | Pathfinding and movement |
| Environment | Terrain, water and hazards |
| Animal AI | Wildlife behavior |
| Migration | External arrivals and travel |
| Governance | Rules, reputation and banishment |
| Earthdale Ledger | Historical records and Social Log |
| Multiplayer | Shared simulation state |

These are logical responsibilities, not mandatory filenames.

Adapt them to the existing project structure.

## Architecture requirements

- Minimize circular dependencies.
- Avoid duplicated state.
- Use centralized event communication where appropriate.
- Keep simulation logic separate from UI.
- Keep decision-making separate from movement execution.
- Keep resource validation separate from NPC intentions.
- Use clear interfaces between systems.
- Make important parameters configurable.
- Ensure state persistence where necessary.
- Avoid unnecessary abstraction and overengineering.

